I mean I love being able to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.320
have conversations with people that&nbsp;
are all working towards the same goal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:18.960
and I’ve kind of started to figure out my method&nbsp;
of directing has kind of changed over the years I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:24.000
used to always think that I had the best ideas and&nbsp;
I had to everybody had to listen to exactly what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:27.760
I think and then I started to go oh my goodness&nbsp;
I have all these really smart people around me&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:33.440
that are brilliant and have invested&nbsp;
their time in this in this vision as well&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:40.160
what I really should do is shape other people's&nbsp;
ideas what I mean so what I started to do&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:47.440
is it's much more collaborative so I have&nbsp;
conversations in more broad strokes with people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:51.920
than see what they bring back to me and then I&nbsp;
start shaping it from there and so I think it's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:57.360
much more collaborative in that sense because&nbsp;
I feel a good director doesn't have to have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.360 --> 00:01:03.040
the best ideas they just have to recognize good&nbsp;
ones and so what I've started to do is I start to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:10.800
direct people to to shape it towards something&nbsp;
that's more what I envisioned but while still&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:14.560
bringing in what they brought to&nbsp;
the table because people come in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:19.680
and they go I got this bag of tools I could&nbsp;
do this I could do this and actors whatever&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:25.840
and you can can you can do that I mean when&nbsp;
I was working with mel on this last movie mel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:32.240
saw the character much funnier than it&nbsp;
was written and and and I really loved&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:36.080
that idea and then him and I kind of started&nbsp;
shaping that character together and I think&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:43.680
a lot of that when people bring ideas to the table&nbsp;
that work for the overall story or or the overall&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:48.960
